But why, really, is permadeath (which I take to be what you mean by the
unusual role of saves) -necessary- in a roguelike?

It's to prevent abuse of the item ID system.  If you could test out an
item and not risk losing it, or any bad effects that came from it, just
reloading the game and naming it what you discovered, much of the
challenge would be gone.  This is especially important in Rogue since
there are a number of items that act as Get Out Of Jail cards (GOOJs?),
like scrolls of scare monsters and wands of slow monster, but it
applies to all rogueslikes.  (Or at least the games that I consider
deserving of the term.)

